<div style="text-align: justify; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">Differences in timing of revenue recognition, billings, and cash collections result in receivables.&#160; Generally, billing occurs subsequent to revenue
          recognition, resulting in unbilled revenue on the balance sheet.&#160; The Company does not receive advances or deposits from customers before revenue is recognized so no contract liabilities are reported.&#160; Accounts receivable are recorded when the
          right to consideration becomes unconditional and are presented separately on the balance sheet.&#160; The changes in accounts receivable and in unbilled revenue were primarily due to normal timing difference between performance and the customer&#8217;s
          payments.</div>
</ix:continuation>
