    </div>
</ix:continuation>
    <ix:continuation id="Text_ce6da795ab2b4683b18f2ee4f611b3342" continuedAt="Text_ce6da795ab2b4683b18f2ee4f611b3343">
<div style="text-align: justify; font-family: 'Times New Roman',Times,serif; font-size: 10pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-weight: normal; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-transform: none;">Based on its
      capital budget, the Company anticipates construction and acquisition expenditures for 2026 and 2027 of approximately $<ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:PurchaseObligationDueInSecondYear" id="Fact_1439643f8718481883d59e1e015b8757" contextRef="c20251231_LongTermPurchaseCommitmentByCategoryOfItemPurchasedAxis_CapitalAdditionsMember" unitRef="U001" decimals="-3" scale="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:PurchaseObligationDueInNextTwelveMonths" id="Fact_3cff4f1ba3674e51a15fd88cb5e2675c" contextRef="c20251231_LongTermPurchaseCommitmentByCategoryOfItemPurchasedAxis_CapitalAdditionsMember" unitRef="U001" decimals="-3" scale="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">48,000</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> in each year, exclusive of any
      acquisitions not yet approved.&#160; The Company plans to finance ongoing capital expenditures with internally-generated funds, borrowings against the Company&#8217;s line of credit, proceeds from the issuance of common stock under its dividend reinvestment and
      direct stock purchase and sale plan and ESPP, potential common stock or debt issues and customer advances and contributions.</div>
</ix:continuation>
